findings.statement:
None of the 7 guide pages in docs/ mentions projections or read models (grep returns 0 for every file). The `rebuild-a-read-model` how-to is still an unchecked item at runbook/phases/22-docs-site.md:75-78. To learn how to build a read model, a reader has three places to go:
- the typed runner's rustdoc, which is behind happenstance's off-by-default `unstable-projection` feature (Cargo.toml:148, lib.rs:196-197 and :237-238);
- the ungated `ProjectionStore` port rustdoc in happenstance-core;
- the example sources (512 to 1,480 lines; transfers-on-sqlite is 663 and rebuilding-read-models is 1,480).

The root README and the site's reference page mention projections only in passing. This is a significant documentation gap for adopters. Calling it "the largest" is an opinion.
